config KLEIN_ENCODER_SLEEP_DISCONNECT
    bool "Disconnect the left encoder pins before deep sleep"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_SLEEP
    help
      The EC11 driver keeps its internal pull-ups on forever, so if the encoder
      rests with a contact closed it leaks current, even in deep sleep. This
      disconnects the A/B pins right before the keyboard powers off. Waking up
      resets the MCU, which reinitializes the encoder normally.

config KLEIN_BATTERY_REPORT_LOWEST
    bool "Report the lower of both halves' battery levels to the host"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_SPLIT_ROLE_CENTRAL && ZMK_BATTERY_REPORTING && ZMK_SPLIT_BLE_CENTRAL_BATTERY_LEVEL_FETCHING && !BT_BAS
    help
      Replaces Zephyr's Battery Service on the central (requires CONFIG_BT_BAS=n)
      with an identical one that reports min(central, peripheral). Hosts like
      macOS only show one battery level per keyboard.
